                <pb facs="0695" n="593" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg593"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/660</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chinese Legation to the
                            Department of State</hi></head>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>[The following translation of a telegram from the Chinese Ministry of Foreign
                        Affairs to the Chinese Chargé was left at the Department by the Chargé,
                        February 4, 1919.]</p>
                </quote>
                <p>The Chinese Government hereby proposes a plan for the complete control and
                    reorganization of the Chinese Eastern Railway.</p>
                <p>It is proposed to appoint, in addition to the Director General, one General
                    Manager for the Railway with executive powers and reorganize all the important
                    Departments by putting foreign engineers now employed by the various Chinese
                    Railways in charge, retaining as many as possible of the American engineers
                    employed by the previous Russian Government and also those employees who are
                    Russians.</p>
                <p>The object of this plan is to maintain the sovereign rights of China and at the
                    same time to render the Railway efficient, in accordance with the American
                    plan.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Peking</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1919-01-30"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">January 30, 1919</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
